From 2aa89193654de5810b5e0b5f5bfbb73bbdeb7cd8 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Ruben Paz <me@ruben.io>
Date: Wed, 10 Jun 2026 21:49:19 +0100
Subject: [PATCH 2/5] power: supply: axp20x_battery: fix voltage_now cache
 assignment (#8)

In axp20x_battery_get_prop(), the POWER_SUPPLY_PROP_VOLTAGE_NOW case
was incorrectly writing to axp20x_batt->current_now instead of
axp20x_batt->voltage_now. This meant voltage_now was never populated
(always 0), causing POWER_SUPPLY_PROP_POWER_NOW to always return 0.

UPower classifies this as an energy-reporting battery (energy_now is
present) and reads the discharge rate directly from power_now, so the
persistent zero caused UPower to report 0W energy-rate with no
time-to-empty/full estimate in GNOME.

Fix the typo so voltage_now is correctly cached.
---
 drivers/power/supply/axp20x_battery.c | 2 +-
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/drivers/power/supply/axp20x_battery.c b/drivers/power/supply/axp20x_battery.c
index abd80d5471c..94938812ba5 100644
--- a/drivers/power/supply/axp20x_battery.c
+++ b/drivers/power/supply/axp20x_battery.c
@@ -424,7 +424,7 @@ static int axp20x_battery_get_prop(struct power_supply *psy,
 
 		/* IIO framework gives mV but Power Supply framework gives uV */
 		val->intval *= 1000;
-		axp20x_batt->current_now = val->intval;
+		axp20x_batt->voltage_now = val->intval;
 
 		break;
 
